  "report_markdown": "## Executive Summary\n\n- The quote from Annie Levin appeared in The New York Observer on 7 Mar. 2022. [9]\n- Jingoism is excessive patriotism or nationalism, especially when marked by a belligerent foreign policy. [9,13,17]\n- Jingoism originated during the Russo-Turkish War. [13]\n- Jingoism originated during the Russo-Turkish War of 1877-1878. [17]\n\n## Findings\n\n### Finding 1: Word of the Day\nThe Merriam-Webster Word of the Day for June 27, 2022, was \"jingoism.\" This is confirmed by multiple accepted claims (01, 02, 05, 09, 13) that consistently identify the word.\n\n### Finding 2: Quoted Writer\nThe writer quoted by Merriam-Webster for the Word of the Day entry from June 27, 2022, was Annie Levin. This is supported by accepted claims (03, 04, 06, 10, 14) that attribute the quote to her.\n\n### Finding 3: Source of the Quote\nThe quote from Annie Levin appeared in *The New York Observer* on March 7, 2022. This is stated in accepted claim 07.\n\n### Finding 4: Definition of Jingoism\nJingoism is defined as excessive patriotism or nationalism, especially when marked by a belligerent foreign policy. This definition is provided in accepted claims (08, 11, 15).\n\n### Finding 5: Origin of Jingoism\nJingoism originated during the Russo-Turkish War of 1877–1878. This is stated in accepted claims (12, 16). Note that claim 12 specifies only \"the Russo-Turkish War,\" while claim 16 provides the fuller date range \"1877–1878.\"\n\n## Evidence Status\n\nAll claims in this report are accepted. The critical claims (01–06, 09–10, 13–14) establish the core facts of the Word of the Day and the quoted writer. The non-critical claims (07–08, 11–12, 15–16) provide supporting details about the quote's source, the definition, and the origin of the term. No claims were rejected or qualified.\n\n## References\n\n1. Lists ofMerriam-Webster'sWordsoftheYear - Wikipedia — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lists_of_Merriam-Webster's_Words_of_the_Year (document: web_search-fdb91df4ff8d00b3)\n2. Merriam-WebsterWordoftheDay: Jingoism — Michael Cavacini — https://michaelcavacini.com/2022/06/27/merriam-webster-word-of-the-day-jingoism/ (document: web_search-785682ef3fe92253)\n3. WordoftheDay: Kiki |Merriam-Webster — https://www.merriam-webster.com/word-of-the-day/kiki-2026-05-16 (document: web_search-f119a035db7aa4d0)\n4. MeriumWebsterWordofTheDay| TikTok — https://www.tiktok.com/discover/merium-webster-word-of-the-day (document: web_search-4511054545ca394b)\n5. Merriam Webster Word Of The Day June 27 2022 Writer — https://www.instagram.com/popular/merriam-webster-word-of-the-day-june-27-2022-writer (document: web_search-041b1ad9bc6f0992)\n6. Merriam-Webster's 2022 Word of the Year, Explained - Thrillist — https://www.thrillist.com/news/nation/merriam-webster-2022-word-of-the-year (document: web_search-a0145e51fc6bfce8)\n7. Word of the Day Calendar | Merriam-Webster — https://www.merriam-webster.com/word-of-the-day/calendar (document: web_search-c07246d9d7a0c561)\n8. Word of the Day: Jingoism | Merriam-Webster — https://www.merriam-webster.com/word-of-the-day/jingoism-2022-06-27 (document: web_search-88a3b8f2e3ab818d)\n9. jingoism by Merriam-Webster's Word of the | Mixcloud — https://www.mixcloud.com/merriam-websterswordoftheday2/jingoism (document: web_search-164f3cc10f373940)\n10. Merriam-Webster Word of the Day: Jingoism — Michael Cavacini — https://michaelcavacini.com/2022/06/27/merriam-webster-word-of-the-day-jingoism (document: web_search-9b9c02d4530d543d)\n11. Merriam-Webster Word of the Day (June 2022) Flashcards — https://quizlet.com/718375852/merriam-webster-word-of-the-day-june-2022-flash-cards (document: web_search-67e4e3a70f053579)\n12. Word of the Day: Jingoism | Merriam-Webster — https://www.merriam-webster.com/word-of-the-day/jingoism-2022-06-27 (document: web_search-f553d4f26f6723f5)\n13. Word of the Day: Jingoism | Merriam-Webster — https://www.merriam-webster.com/word-of-the-day/jingoism-2022-06-27 (document: web_search-fc728a0beca24673)\n14. JINGOISM Definition & Meaning — https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/jingoism (document: web_search-af01239fc52f9750)\n15. JINGOISM Synonyms: 10 Similar and Opposite Words | Merriam-Webster Thesaurus — https://www.merriam-webster.com/thesaurus/jingoism (document: web_search-822110301c1942fe)\n16. Merriam-Webster Word of the Day: Jingoism — https://michaelcavacini.com/2022/06/27/merriam-webster-word-of-the-day-jingoism (document: web_search-19913a0d871eac49)\n17. Merriam-Webster Word of the Day: Jingoism — Michael CavaciniMichael Cavacini — https://michaelcavacini.com/2022/06/27/merriam-webster-word-of-the-day-jingoism/ (document: fetch_page-43ada9dd2473589e)\n\n## Claim Register\n\n- (accepted, critical=false) The quote from Annie Levin appeared in The New York Observer on 7 Mar. 2022. [9]\n- (accepted, critical=false) Jingoism is excessive patriotism or nationalism, especially when marked by a belligerent foreign policy. [9,13,17]\n- (qualified, critical=false) Jingoism originated during the Russo-Turkish War. [13]\n- (qualified, critical=false) Jingoism originated during the Russo-Turkish War of 1877-1878. [17]\n",
